WEBVTT

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.370
Don't let him get away!

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.610
Get ahead of him and cut him off!

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.490
What's all this fuss?

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.820
Look, I'm a ninja!

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.260
Try and get away from this, Escape King!

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.060
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:06.500
<b>Episode Sixteen
The Great Plan to Infiltrate the Asahikawa 7th Division!!</b>

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.980
Shiraishi was captured by the 7th Division?

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:07.640
Was it Lt. Tsurumi?

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:11.000
No, I didn't see Lt. Tsurumi.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.150
It was another unit.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:17.400
According to the locals, they were 
on their way back to Asahikawa.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:23.530
There were too many for me to try a 
head-on attempt to rescue Shiraishi.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:28.660
But we'll have serious problems if he's 
taken all the way to their HQ in Asahikawa.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:32.210
Knowing Shiraishi, can't he 
just get away on his own?

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:37.300
Maybe he's been killed, and they're 
flaying him as we speak!

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.960
If they lock him away somewhere in their HQ,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:43.640
it might take him months 
to get out on his own.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:47.780
Nagakura, Ienaga, wait for 
Sugimoto's group to return here.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:51.100
Once they arrive, head to Asahikawa.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:55.110
Kiroranke and I will get Shiraishi back!

00:02:55.110 --> 00:03:02.450
He's the only one who can enter 
Abashiri Prison and contact Nopperabo.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:06.410
<b>Jintan</b>

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:06.410
<b>Jintan</b>

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:06.410
<b>Iwamizawa</b>

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:10.150
You've already met the person 
you're fated to be with.

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:12.370
Who? Who is it?

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.340
What is it that you sell, merchant?

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.920
I don't sell anything.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.130
Your friend there is a fortune-teller, huh?

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:23.590
Lucky guy... I want to be the gigolo 
for a pretty girl like that, too.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:26.610
Gigolo? I'm not a gigolo...

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.060
Inkarmat, give me money!

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.760
There's a bean candy seller here!

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:36.230
Three men with a little Ainu girl?

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.740
I saw them in Yuubari.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:44.380
There were these three nasty-looking 
men who tried to sell me a liver.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:47.490
That guy with the hat was probably 
some kind of terrible criminal!

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.090
I can tell these things!

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.500
<b>Otaru</b>

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.500
<b>Sapporo</b>

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.500
<b>Iwamizawa</b>

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.500
<b>Yuubari</b>

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.500
<b>Ashibetsu</b>

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:53.880
Yuubari, huh?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.850
I should've guessed.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.060
If you take the fastest route 
to Abashiri from Otaru,

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.130
you run into Asahikawa.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:14.650
<b>Yuubari</b>

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:14.650
<b>Abashiri</b>

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:05.030
Asahikawa is the 7th's base of operations.

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:14.650
<b>Asahikawa</b>

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.710
I thought they'd go around it.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.140
If they passed through Yuubari,

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:14.650
<b>Tokachi
 Region</b>

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.780
maybe they passed through the Daisetsuzan
Volcanic Group and the Hidaka Mountains,

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.650
and headed to Tokachi.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.750
Tokap?

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.060
Tokachi.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.150
What's tokap?

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.010
It means "boobs."

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:23.530
Tokap! Tokap!

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.740
Cikapasi, enough of that.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:27.240
Tokap!

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:30.950
Stop glancing back at Inkarmat, Cikapasi!

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:37.330
Look!

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:42.460
We've been waiting for you.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:45.490
I've got news. Bad news.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:46.760
What is it?

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.720
Let's hurry! We need to get ahead of them!

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.090
How do we get him back?

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:55.460
Strike the 7th in their sleep?

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.360
Blast a few of them with a bomb 
to throw the rest into chaos—

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.190
Is that how you fought at the Amur River?

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:06.150
Why did you abandon your 
home and come to Hokkaido?

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:12.450
Or did the czar's men chase you here?
 You and Nopperabo both.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:17.710
Do you know Nopperabo's real name?

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:24.090
<b>Mikawa Village</b>

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:28.050
Give one sen to the Inari in that alleyway,

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:32.470
and pay your respects. Once Osen arrives

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:37.730
at the tea shop and has a seat, 
serve her some bitter tea.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:35.150
A bean candy seller!

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.730
I want some! Can I buy some?

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.730
Give me bean candy!

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.150
Thanks for your purchase.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:51.460
After the bitter tea...

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.450
<b>Kamuy Kotan
Hanging Bridge</b>

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.450
Kamuy Kotan?

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:58.890
The Kamuy Kotan is the domain of the gods.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:01.980
<b>Kamuy Kotan</b>

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:02.640
It's always been said that 
humans have no place there.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.250
To the Ainu, this valley is a 
dangerous source of many accidents.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.930
They've always feared those accidents 
as the work of an evil god.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:13.660
So there's lots of interesting 
stories about the Kamuy Kotan.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.850
Stories of katanas that devour men.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.060
Katanas that devour men?

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:20.150
The Ipetam.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:24.660
The Ipetam is a cursed sword that flies 
through the air in search of men to prey on.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:28.070
Bury it in the mountains, 
throw it in a deep river,

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.590
and it will come back anyway.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:34.180
Bury it in a coffin with rocks, and it 
will eat the rocks with a crunching sound.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:38.710
But once the rocks are gone it will leave 
the coffin and start to attack people,

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:42.880
so in the end, they threw it in the 
bottomless swamp of the Kamuy Kotan.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.880
And then it didn't come back.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.440
I see.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:52.040
Then I shall be an Ipetam. One that 
climbed out of the bottomless swamp.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.760
Cross ten at a time!

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:06.360
<i>Kamuy Kotan. Hanging bridge...</i>

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.580
<i>What are they going to do?</i>

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.620
<i>You've gotta be kidding me!</i>

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:24.460
<i>Sure, we're on a bridge, but is he still 
going to fight this many people with a katana?</i>

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.970
You stupid old man!

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:39.230
Bridge collapse! Several men fell!

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:40.730
Turn back! We're going to save them!

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.570
I'm gonna die! Somebody save me!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.980
Shiraishi!

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.400
Don't let go!

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.530
Shiraishi!

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:54.030
Kiro-chan!

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.530
Just wait!

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:57.710
Grab on!

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:00.160
I could get rid of these any time I wanted!

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:02.830
Shit!

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.290
Shiraishi, hang in there!

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.250
Almost there! Reach out!

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:08.750
Come on, Shiraishi!

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.720
What's wrong? Hurry!

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.140
Shiraishi!

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:48.750
I believe he's already 
arrived at Asahikawa by now.

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:52.320
Even if he can escape on his own,

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:57.220
we can't wait for him when we don't 
know how long that will take.

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:00.780
We don't even know if he can.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.330
He may be the Escape King,

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:04.140
but that's not a prison.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.870
Who knows what they're doing to him?

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.940
They may be flaying him right now!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.270
You go look, Ogata.

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:14.170
You're with the 7th, right?

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:16.200
I'm considered a deserter right now.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.760
What about you, Kiroranke?

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:19.390
You were with the 7th, right?

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:22.080
They saw my face at the Kamuy Kotan.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.560
<i>Well, I guess it's okay.</i>

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.310
We've got a copy of his tattoos.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:47.320
No, I want to save him.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:54.610
He's a ridiculous man, but there's 
still uses for Shiraishi.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.160
But how do we save him?

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.140
Knowing that man...

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:09.000
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:13.770
Nikaidou, let go!

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:15.540
Give me that vial!

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:17.670
No!

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.640
What's all this fuss, Sergeant Tsukishima?

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.030
Lt. Tsurumi!

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:25.600
No!

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:31.060
Nikaidou stole a whole vial of morphine,
and was taking extra doses of it in secret!

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.770
Don't blame me if he dies from an overdose.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.380
Nikaidou, you know better than that.

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:39.370
You need to follow the doctor's orders.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:40.200
Give it back.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.910
No, Nikaidou! Bad!

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:46.560
Youhei's right leg burned.

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:48.630
Along with Edogai-kun's house.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.750
I can't track down Sugimoto without a leg.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:56.170
Nikaidou, it's not right to just give up.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:57.320
No!

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.680
Nikaidou, no! No!

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.560
Lt. Tsurumi, somebody's there.

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:11.670
Who are you?

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:13.730
You want to know who I am?

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:17.280
I'm the one who made that 
rifle you're carrying!

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:19.920
Lt. General Arisaka, sir!

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:21.780
I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.450
<i>Arisaka!</i>

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:26.360
<i>The genius weapons designer.</i>

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:27.510
<i>A lieutenant general in the army.</i>

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:28.790
<i>Arisaka Narizou!</i>

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:30.370
I'm sorry, sir!

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.580
How've you been, Tsurumi-kun?

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.710
I see you're doing well, sir!

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:40.600
Lt. General Arisaka's lost much of his 
hearing after spending years making weapons.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:41.560
I see.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:44.640
How was Asahikawa?

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.910
Asahikawa's made a hot air 
balloon unit of their own,

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:50.920
and they want to put 
some kind of weapon on it!

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:55.490
Those things use hydrogen to float.
 One puncture and they're done for,

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:57.300
so recon is the most you'll 
ever get out of them!

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.230
And they're slow, too!

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:02.130
The age of airplanes is upon us!

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:06.030
<b>Morphine</b>

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:06.030
Is that morphine, Tsurumi-kun?

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:09.280
Does your head wound still bother you?

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:11.900
Actually, Tsurumi-kun, has your
 attempt to grow poppies

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:14.120
that can thrive in cold 
climates gotten anywhere?

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:17.690
I'm trying to get money so I can 
expand the size of the fields.

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:19.430
Opium makes money!

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:22.280
International opinion has 
turned against England,

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.770
and they're getting out of 
the opium business, you see.

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:29.320
Lt. General Arisaka, please don't 
tell people about the poppy fields.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:35.090
<i>Lt. General Arisaka came all the 
way to Otaru to see Lt. Tsurumi?</i>

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:38.110
<i>There's no end to how deep 
the rabbit hole goes with him.</i>

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:41.140
I've brought the latest in 
domestically-produced weaponry.

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:43.050
A Type-38 machine gun and 
Type-38 infantry rifle,

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:46.570
developed by Nambu-kun, one of my men!

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:49.370
Beautiful...

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:53.100
The beauty of the gun 
testifies to its function.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:55.040
You'll sell a million!

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:00.500
But the more that sell,
the more people will die!

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.800
This is a cursed business I'm in!

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:08.650
The things you make 
are beautiful, so make them!

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.680
Beauty and power are one and the same.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:15.320
In search of functional beauty, 
you created a powerful weapon.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:17.720
And that which is beautiful 
should be praised!

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:24.080
The 28 centimeter howitzers were gorgeous!

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:29.160
The fire support they provided did not 
discriminate between friend and foe.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.400
It ripped apart the bodies of young men,

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:34.060
and made the skies rain with gore and blood!

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:37.690
I ran through those rains of blood,

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:41.040
and it was beautiful!

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.620
Your head is messed up, Tsurumi-kun!

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:46.770
Correct! I'm missing my frontal lobes!

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:54.870
<i>A large war will increase
 demand for painkillers...</i>

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:56.310
<b>Morphine</b>

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:58.810
<i>And Japan's high-quality weapons, too.</i>

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:02.020
<i>That's what the Ainu gold will be used for.</i>

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:05.560
Bang! Bang! Bang!

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:05.340
<i>War will bring jobs to 
the people of Hokkaido.</i>

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:05.340
Bap-bap-bap.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.890
<i>More wars will need to keep happening.</i>

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:07.890
It doesn't go bap-bap-bap!

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:10.530
Get 'em! Shoot 'em all up!

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:10.530
<i>It's a war addiction!</i>

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:14.320
Bears attack humans with overwhelming power.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.520
But who blames the bear?

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:17.580
Other bears.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:21.670
One of my men was attacked by 
a bear, and this is what he said!

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:24.500
"It was a beautiful creature."

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.460
That's an interesting guy 
you've got working for you!

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.610
Lt. General Arisaka!

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:31.010
He's very depressed right now!

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:35.570
I know it's asking a lot, but do 
you suppose you could help him?

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:40.440
<b>Several Days Later</b>

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:40.440
You stole it again, huh?

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.330
Give it back!

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.090
I'll tell Lt. Tsurumi on you!

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:45.650
Give it here!

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:47.440
Nikaidou!

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.030
You've got a wonderful visitor!

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:52.870
A visitor? Who?

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.920
Come in, sir!

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:00.000
Who's that?

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:02.000
Who is it?

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:05.350
Who... who are you?

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:06.800
I'm scared!

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:08.660
Who the hell are you?

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:09.800
Get lost!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.800
So you're Nikaidou-kun, huh?!

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:14.680
Who's this?

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.640
I've come to give you a present!

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.520
A present? What is it?

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:22.610
I hope you like it!

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:28.110
Your new leg!

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.770
Aw, it's just a fake leg.

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:35.030
Not just <i>any</i> fake leg, though!

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:43.200
I made it on short notice, but it's 
got room for three rounds of buckshot.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:46.930
I could've put in more 
if I used rifle bullets,

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:51.570
but a weapon like this is only useful at 
close quarters and in a surprise situation.

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:54.800
If you want to make sure you 
stop an opponent at short range,

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.890
buckshot's the way to go!

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:00.390
Thank you, person I don't know!

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:02.980
What are you doing? This is a hospital!

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:10.370
Congratulations on your 
wonderful new leg, Nikaidou!

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:16.370
<b>Outskirts of Asahikawa</b>

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.370
Who the hell is this?

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:20.830
His name is Suzukawa Kiyohiro. 
He's a marriage fraudster.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.080
A genius at disguise.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:25.070
We met in Abashiri.

00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:26.790
Abashiri?

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:30.510
You were hiding that?

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:35.260
I didn't say I'd share every 
bit of information I had.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:38.470
You didn't tell me either, old man.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:42.730
Don't worry. I was intending to 
meet him on the way to Abashiri.

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:45.650
You crafty old geezer...

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:49.650
What can a marriage fraudster do?

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:52.500
Fraud involves the use of the brain.

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:59.660
Don't compare me to a violent prison escapee,
 who steals things from others by force.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:02.380
So, what do you want me to do?

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:05.790
Save Shiraishi from the 7th.

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:10.550
We won't know where in the 7th's 
Asahikawa Barracks he's being kept

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:14.340
unless someone gets in.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:17.050
So I pretend to be one of them?

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:20.840
After the incident at the Kamuy Kotan,
 they'll be on their guard.

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:25.140
You'd have to be someone important 
to get them to tell you.

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:28.280
One of the upper brass from 
the division in Tokyo?

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:32.120
No, the further up in the military you get, 
the more you know the people around you.

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:34.360
A fictional officer would
 be found out instantly.

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:37.320
A dog (inu)?

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:40.660
How about Inudou Shirosuke?

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:44.080
Inudou? The Warden of Abashiri Prison?

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.450
Do they look similar?

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:47.790
Nope.

00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:56.990
The odds of anyone in the 7th knowing 
the Warden of Abashiri are low.

00:17:56.990 --> 00:17:58.290
But unless you look almost identical,

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:01.830
someone who knows him will 
see through the disguise.

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:02.470
Will this work?

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:05.380
Inudou is stern and fastidious.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:07.310
He's obsessed with following rules,

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:12.480
but also willing to secretly lock me 
up forever out of personal hatred.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:15.820
His twisted nature appears on his face.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:19.700
It's true. Your personality 
shows on your face.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.190
For instance, if you see a 
bear with a face like a fox,

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:24.460
it's one that's got a nasty temper.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:26.650
Right, Asirpa-san?

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:31.250
No good. It's past her bedtime.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.590
How about this, then?

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:47.270
So, how will you fool the 7th now that 
you look like the Warden of Abashiri?

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:49.960
Don't be in such a hurry.

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.730
I have an idea.

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:54.170
I'll let you handle the rest.

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:03.160
Leave her be. She's nasty when she's sleepy.

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:06.440
Hah! She'll be a fine woman someday.

00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:12.900
What's wrong?

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:21.250
I just remembered...

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:26.560
You're the old man who showed up at 
the herring longhouse, aren't you?

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:32.020
Was Shiraishi working with you?

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.900
Shiraishi was working with them?

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:37.650
Yeah. If that's true, it probably 
started a while ago.

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:42.300
When Shiraishi reached out to grab my hand,

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:44.120
I saw a clear hesitation.

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:48.040
Given the situation, 
can't you look past that?

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:51.540
So you admit it, then.

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:57.550
There are no enemies or allies here. 
All that's important is information.

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:01.290
He probably figured you'd 
kill him if you found out.

00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:04.380
That'd be just like him.

00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:07.560
What will you do? Will you still save him?

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:09.930
And then kill him when you do?

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:14.930
Someone who betrays you once will 
betray you again and again.

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:16.690
Sugimoto...

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:20.690
Don't kill anyone you don't have to.

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:29.030
<i>Asahikawa, the military city.</i>

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:35.060
<b>Asahikawa</b>

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:32.200
<i>As the czar's forces tried to sweep south,</i>

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:34.510
<i>fortifying it became a critical mission.</i>

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:38.220
<i>The establishment of railway tracks 
and a 7th Division garrison</i>

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:41.900
<i>made it one of the largest cities in 
Hokkaido at the time, after Hakodate,</i>

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:44.390
<i>Otaru, and Sapporo.</i>

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:50.220
The 7th's base is huge. Where is he?

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:55.520
It's not a prison, so it can't be 
that hard to get on base, but...

00:20:55.860 --> 00:21:00.120
There's no way we can check 
out each individual building.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:03.300
Should we make them hand 
Shiraishi over to us?

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:11.000
The insignia number of the men 
who took Shiraishi was "27."

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:14.410
That's one of the four infantry 
regiments at Asahikawa...

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:17.450
The 27th Infantry Regiment.

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:19.830
This is their barracks.

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:22.760
Wait a second. The 27th?

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:23.920
What is it, Ogata?

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:26.630
Are you guys idiots?

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:29.100
Oh, right!

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:32.810
So they're in the same 
regiment as Lt. Tsurumi?

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:38.020
It's very likely that the 
27th is hiding Shiraishi.

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:43.990
The regiment is lead by Lt. Colonel Yodogawa,
 who's under Lt. Tsurumi's control.

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.990
<b>Lt. Colonel Yodogawa Terunaka</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.990
What? The Warden of Abashiri
 wants to meet me?

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:51.410
What does he want?

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:57.490
I am Inudou Shirosuke,
 the Warden of Abashiri Prison.

00:21:57.490 --> 00:21:58.880
Nice to meet you.

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:04.960
Inudou...

00:23:35.370 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time:
Inside the Belly</b>

00:23:35.960 --> 00:23:39.480
Next Time: "Inside the Belly."
